{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792945818,"nonce":"sONVhROIQAlv29BOdbE6cusBYQ8=","title":"A page agent carries the session's WebSocket to an Ash program","message":"Ash's browser host exposes no socket or fetch (ashui-4e). A page agent, like xwindow.mjs and gpu.mjs (page JS on the main thread, talking over shared-memory rings, waking the loop on events), would own the WebSocket and the local-first Yjs documents (web/session/src/client.js) and hand the Haxe side messages. Needs ash-7d's view on the ring protocol and on waking a program that sits in await. Blocks the page implementation of the Workspace interface.\n\nPart of the browser epic: git-bug ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382","files":null}]}